  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d29ab41979ff4944b90c0c99eeb75f12, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Facts:
  - Eating cooked alcohol can still raise your BAC level, and can show up on a breathalyzer
    test.
  - A 2025 poll of drivers from Vancouver found that only 13% reported driving more
    cautiously when seeing a "baby on board" sticker.
  - More than 1.2 million people die in road traffic crashes every year.
  - Correctly used seat-belts reduce the risk of death in a crash by 61%.
  - Helmets reduce fatal and serious head injuries by up to 45%.
  - In Washington, using a fake passenger in an HOV lane brings an extra $200 penalty
    on top of the $186 fine.
  - Drivers who have been awake for 17 hours pose the same amount of risk as they
    would if they had a blood alcohol content reading of 0.05
  - In 2010, an anonymous motorist was fined 290,000 Swiss francs, equaling about 
    $300,000 USD!
  - Going significantly under the speed limit is just as dangerous as going over
    the speed limit.
  text: {fileID: 9055153206642208702}
